WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:01.126
- [Joe Hampton:] You know, there's a difference

00:00:01.126 --> 00:00:04.921
between a kid who can play
basketball and a hooper.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.841
You know, a hooper is someone
who can go get a bucket

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:10.635
at any given time for his team.

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:13.430
Someone just playing basketball
just knows the fundamentals

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.265
and just plays basketball the right way.

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:16.266
I guess there's nothing wrong with that,

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:18.893
but I'm a hooper for sure, for sure.

00:00:21.062 --> 00:00:23.982
- [Eric Yeboah:] I wonder how it is that,

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:26.693
cuz you've had one of the more unique stories

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.695
out of everybody on the team with just, like, this 

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.947
kinda like reintroduction to the world, right?

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:33.158
Everybody saw you on the
national stage in high school,

00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:34.951
Oak Hill, what you did, and
now it's not, you know,

00:00:34.951 --> 00:00:36.661
now you're reintroducing
yourself to a new world.

00:00:36.661 --> 00:00:39.664
What was that like
getting comfortable also

00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:41.916
with just, like, telling
your story about what

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:44.085
you've been through over
the last couple of years?

00:00:45.253 --> 00:00:48.882
- [Hampton:] I mean, even though I
was, I've been through a lot,

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.592
a lot of ups and downs, like you said,

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:52.510
a lot of people knew who I was before,

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.971
and that's why I'm reintroducing myself.

00:00:54.971 --> 00:00:57.348
But it was really easy

00:00:57.348 --> 00:00:59.559
for me to open up to the camera crew

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:03.188
and tell my story because
they made it easy for us.

00:01:03.188 --> 00:01:04.397
They were good people.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.733
They were cool. They were open.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.485
They told some of their stories.

00:01:09.944 --> 00:01:12.697
And ultimately, I got comfortable

00:01:12.697 --> 00:01:14.491
with telling my story because
they were real, and they were

00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:18.036
good people. And it
just made it that much easier.

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:19.996
- The other things that you took

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:21.623
from that experience that you were, like,

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:24.959
hey, at the end of
the day, I needed that.

00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:26.419
And like, what are others,

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.670
some of those other things
where you're like, yeah,

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:28.505
I definitely needed that experience

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:30.465
because it taught me this, this and this?

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:33.593
- Of course, [John] Mosley, in general, I mean,

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:37.013
I needed him too. He was a lifesaver.

00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:39.265
God put him in my life for a reason
- [Yeboah:] Mmhmm.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.017
- [Hampton:] at the perfect time.

00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:45.605
And just everything that he
taught me with, like I said,

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:50.610
responding in the right way,
with not lashing out,

00:01:51.027 --> 00:01:55.448
with just praying and just
seein' that, like, I'm OK.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.284
And that if I do things the
right way that I'll be fine.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:04.707
So Mosley, like, I needed him.
- [Yeboah:] Yeah.
- [Hampton:] For real. He saved my life.

00:02:04.999 --> 00:02:07.460
- [John Mosley:] Don't put on a show. 
You win the game.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.505
Don't put on a show. You
freakin' win the game.

00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:12.048
You don't put on the show.

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:16.010
You win! You get in the paint,
and you finish, and you win,

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.595
and you defend, you rebound,

00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:20.140
and you play together. Come on!

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.391
- Let's go, let's get it.
- Let's go, let's go.

00:02:22.225 --> 00:02:23.393
- [Mosley:] Hey, on three. 1, 2, 3, win!

00:02:23.393 --> 00:02:25.895
- [Yeboah:] With the JUCO
experience in general,

00:02:25.895 --> 00:02:27.230
I think a lot of people don't even know

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.064
that with a lot of the players

00:02:28.064 --> 00:02:30.275
that there are so many sacrifices
that people end up there.

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:32.402
Everybody's not just
there because of grades.

00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:34.654
Sometimes it's just sacrifice.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.364
And I think even for you, like,

00:02:36.364 --> 00:02:38.408
is that something you also
realized when you were there,

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:39.951
like, just hearing other stories

00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:41.161
of other players and how they got there?

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:45.081
It's like, "Oh, they all have
similar stories or at least have

00:02:45.081 --> 00:02:49.127
all been through something
while we're here," you know what I mean?

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:50.211
- Yeah, nah, really,

00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:52.463
I mean, in that moment,
cuz Mosley, he was

00:02:52.463 --> 00:02:55.592
gettin' on us about how we
weren't givin' it our all

00:02:55.592 --> 00:02:59.012
and complaining
- Mmm.
- about not doing the extra.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:03.474
And for him, it was like,
you're gonna come every day,

00:03:03.474 --> 00:03:04.559
you're gonna give it your all

00:03:04.559 --> 00:03:06.269
cuz ultimately you don't want to be here.

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:07.729
You don't wanna be in this place.

00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:10.148
I don't want you here cuz you
need to be at the next level.

00:03:10.148 --> 00:03:11.399
We wanna get you to the next level.

00:03:11.399 --> 00:03:12.692
So you're going to do
everything
- Yeah.
- you're supposed to

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.235
to get to that level.

00:03:14.235 --> 00:03:15.653
And at that point, he had enough

00:03:15.653 --> 00:03:18.740
of us complaining, and he felt as if

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.742
we weren't giving it
our all and all of that.

00:03:20.742 --> 00:03:24.078
So he was saying that
- Yeah.
- "I'm the one who's sacrificing to be in here.

00:03:24.078 --> 00:03:27.624
I'm missing my daughter's softball game

00:03:27.624 --> 00:03:30.126
and my son's practices, all of that stuff,

00:03:30.126 --> 00:03:32.170
and you're complaining to me."

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.839
And, like, I felt, I mean, we understood.

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:36.341
We felt what he was talking about.

00:03:36.341 --> 00:03:39.219
And in that moment we decided to

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:42.680
to reconvene and come as
a group, as the guys,

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.642
and get it together and do
the lift and get outta there.

00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:48.603
But he was just trying
to make a point that,

00:03:49.687 --> 00:03:51.189
I mean, you don't want
to be in this place.

00:03:51.189 --> 00:03:53.441
The JUCO grind is real.

00:03:53.441 --> 00:03:56.194
So you have to work just

00:03:56.194 --> 00:03:58.154
that much harder just to get out,

00:03:58.154 --> 00:04:00.198
you know what I'm saying?
- [Yeboah:] Yeah.
- [Hampton:] And that's tough.

00:04:00.198 --> 00:04:03.117
- [Mosley:] Kid like Joe,
he knows how to play.

00:04:03.117 --> 00:04:06.037
So I have to give him a chance

00:04:06.037 --> 00:04:10.583
until he is a detriment to
everybody else in the program.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.417
- [Yeboah:] It was also like,

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.502
I'm not gonna give up on you either.

00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:14.921
So whatever it takes
for me to get you back,

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:17.966
I'm gonna go do it, which
is a shoutout to him for that.
- Right.

00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:18.925
- That's nice stuff.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:19.759
Do you have another one?

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.719
I know you said there was another one too.

00:04:21.719 --> 00:04:22.553
- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:22.553 --> 00:04:24.722
There's, I mean, there's
another good story,

00:04:24.722 --> 00:04:26.599
like an inspirational story,

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.685
like as far as coaching. When I first came

00:04:28.685 --> 00:04:33.398
to ELAC, I transferred
from Pasadena City College,

00:04:33.398 --> 00:04:35.441
and my grades weren't good. I
was originally supposed to go

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:38.736
to Long Beach State from
Pasadena City College in 2017.

00:04:38.736 --> 00:04:39.946
My grades weren't good enough.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:40.780
I was slacking.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.490
This was one of the times
I was a knucklehead,

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.576
open cases and stuff,
on the run, all of that.

00:04:45.576 --> 00:04:48.871
And when I got the call
and someone told me like,

00:04:48.871 --> 00:04:52.041
"Yo, go to Coach Mosley,
he'll help you out.

00:04:52.041 --> 00:04:54.544
You go up there and just
do what you gotta do."
- Mmm.

00:04:54.544 --> 00:04:56.045
- The meeting went great.

00:04:56.045 --> 00:04:59.382
I got enrolled to school
and got into classes.

00:04:59.382 --> 00:05:01.634
He told me about the guys. I met the guys.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.053
Then I started to work out and practice.

00:05:04.053 --> 00:05:05.805
I'm expecting to play.

00:05:07.515 --> 00:05:11.060
Right?
- [Yeboah laughing]
- I'm expecting to...I'm practicing.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.563
Practice uniform, going
to school, going to class.

00:05:14.522 --> 00:05:17.483
Now I was, to be honest,
I'm slacking here and there.

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:20.528
Not showing up, doing my
usual slacking here and there,

00:05:20.528 --> 00:05:24.032
but I'm in school and
going to class or whatever.

00:05:24.032 --> 00:05:27.952
And he hits me with the, "You're
not playing this season.

00:05:27.952 --> 00:05:30.872
You're here to get your
grades up and do what

00:05:30.872 --> 00:05:33.166
you're supposed to off the court
- [Yeboah:] Mmm.
- [Hampton:] And

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:35.585
we'll worry about the court next year."

00:05:35.585 --> 00:05:40.131
So my first time touching the
court was this past season,

00:05:40.131 --> 00:05:42.300
"Last Chance U," what you seen.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.219
- Oh, I got you. OK. OK. That wasn't

00:05:45.219 --> 00:05:47.347
initially what you thought
it was going to be like.

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:49.599
You thought I was going to play, like, got you.

00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:52.477
- I'm thinking I was going
to play at least two years

00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:55.229
to get, you know what I'm saying?
- And bounce. Yeah, yeah.
- I wanted to get playin'.

00:05:56.814 --> 00:06:00.276
You know, but he did the extra
- Yeah.
- to make sure that

00:06:00.276 --> 00:06:03.738
I will be good now, you feel me?
- Yeah.

00:06:03.738 --> 00:06:04.572
- It's not even me, Coach.

00:06:04.572 --> 00:06:05.948
- Listen.

00:06:05.948 --> 00:06:08.034
- I'm working hard.
- Listen. I know.
- I'm working hard for the team out there!

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:10.161
- Hey, listen, listen. And you are.

00:06:10.161 --> 00:06:11.996
- [Yeboah:] What steps did you have to take?

00:06:11.996 --> 00:06:13.748
I think a lot of people don't understand

00:06:13.748 --> 00:06:15.875
that in between part, where it's like,

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:19.253
I have to now adjust, you know,
I did Penn State.

00:06:19.253 --> 00:06:21.339
Then I did another
college, and now I'm here.

00:06:21.339 --> 00:06:24.509
What is it like trying to
gather yourself and be like,

00:06:24.509 --> 00:06:26.427
this is now the route that I have to go,

00:06:26.427 --> 00:06:27.929
and I have to accept what it is

00:06:27.929 --> 00:06:29.764
and what it's going to be like

00:06:29.764 --> 00:06:32.100
so I can get to where I'm trying to go?

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.352
- It's a lot. It's a lot.

00:06:34.352 --> 00:06:36.187
It's a toll mentally, really.

00:06:36.187 --> 00:06:38.773
Because you really, you
have times where you

00:06:38.773 --> 00:06:42.193
feel like, is this
really what I want to do?

00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:45.780
Cuz I mean, like you said
- Mmhmm.
- I was at university, at Oak Hill

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.616
and I was playing this high-quality
D-I basketball

00:06:48.616 --> 00:06:50.535
with all these good players.

00:06:50.535 --> 00:06:51.452
And then I'll take a step back, and

00:06:51.452 --> 00:06:53.246
I'm playing JUCO basketball.

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:55.665
Not necessarily bad
players. Still good players,

00:06:55.665 --> 00:06:58.084
but it's not the same level of basketball.
- [Yeboah:] Yeah.

00:06:58.084 --> 00:07:01.546
- [Hampton:] It's not the same clique that
I'm used to playing with.

00:07:01.546 --> 00:07:04.882
And it was days where, like, I felt like

00:07:04.882 --> 00:07:07.844
I wasn't getting any better
or going anywhere with it.

00:07:07.844 --> 00:07:10.054
And it was taking a toll on me mentally.

00:07:10.054 --> 00:07:12.557
And I had to really sit
down and think if like

00:07:12.557 --> 00:07:14.225
this is really what
I want to do.
- Yeah.
- If this

00:07:14.225 --> 00:07:19.230
is what I love, then I'm going
to fight adversity head-on,

00:07:19.355 --> 00:07:21.482
and I'mma push through
it because it's light at

00:07:21.482 --> 00:07:23.025
the end of that tunnel.

00:07:23.025 --> 00:07:24.735
- Y'all was going to win it too.

00:07:24.735 --> 00:07:28.990
But you know what I'm
sayin'? That's how it goes.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:32.326
Best team. Appreciate each
and every one of y'all.

00:07:32.326 --> 00:07:34.745
- [Yeboah:] You know, how we
saw how once COVID

00:07:34.745 --> 00:07:37.707
canceled the tournament
for you guys, state,

00:07:37.707 --> 00:07:39.000
I think everybody can agree

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.294
that that was one of the toughest finales

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:44.088
of any show that we've watched
from a viewer standpoint.

00:07:44.088 --> 00:07:47.842
But being in it, like, what was
that like, just knowing

00:07:47.842 --> 00:07:50.428
that you guys have put in so
much work, and then, you know,

00:07:50.428 --> 00:07:51.762
it was done just like that?

00:07:51.762 --> 00:07:54.432
What do you remember
from that moment the most?

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.603
- I just remember how
bad we wanted to win.

00:07:58.603 --> 00:08:02.773
We worked for playing in
the state championship game.
- Mmhmm.

00:08:02.773 --> 00:08:04.317
- That's what our goal was.

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:05.902
And everything that we
did leading up to it

00:08:05.902 --> 00:08:09.363
was for that purpose, and
to get all the way up

00:08:09.363 --> 00:08:12.825
to that point. And

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:15.703
no one did anything to affect it.

00:08:15.703 --> 00:08:18.623
It's just, like, a natural thing.

00:08:18.623 --> 00:08:20.708
Like, just something
that we can't control.

00:08:20.708 --> 00:08:22.502
It was hard.

00:08:22.502 --> 00:08:25.046
And to take that, it was tough.
- Yeah.

00:08:25.046 --> 00:08:28.508
- You had emotions flowin' crazy.
Coach cried.

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:30.343
We, some of the players cried.

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:31.385
I cried.

00:08:31.385 --> 00:08:33.596
What we wanted... state championship.
- Yeah.

00:08:33.596 --> 00:08:34.889
- It was a waste.

00:08:35.723 --> 00:08:38.184
- Nah, nah, and it shows, like right after that,

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:40.478
like you have an abrupt ending.

00:08:40.478 --> 00:08:43.898
And then, I forgot who
mentioned it, but it's also, like,

00:08:43.898 --> 00:08:46.192
that affects a lot of
everybody's, like, recruiting

00:08:46.192 --> 00:08:47.735
or, you know, maybe college looks

00:08:47.735 --> 00:08:49.487
that maybe woulda helped other people.

00:08:49.487 --> 00:08:50.821
So it's done like that,

00:08:50.821 --> 00:08:52.949
and then now we're just
sitting around chillin' for

00:08:52.949 --> 00:08:54.408
the next whatever amount of months,

00:08:54.408 --> 00:08:57.161
not knowing where you gotta head to next.

00:08:57.161 --> 00:08:58.788
Do you remember those
in between months

00:08:58.788 --> 00:09:01.165
between, you know, after it ended and before?

00:09:01.165 --> 00:09:04.418
What was it like just chilling, waiting?

00:09:05.545 --> 00:09:09.590
- Do I? I wasn't chillin',
I was panicking, bro.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:13.678
I was panicking. Like I, because
for me, I wanted to be

00:09:13.678 --> 00:09:15.221
a Division I basketball
player. I wanted to

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:18.933
get back to that stage,
to where I belong.

00:09:18.933 --> 00:09:21.227
And I didn't wanna sell myself short.

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:22.562
I wasn't going Division II.

00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:25.815
I wasn't going D-III. And no
disrespect to those programs

00:09:25.815 --> 00:09:29.694
and those leagues or whatever,
I just couldn't do it there.

00:09:29.694 --> 00:09:31.362
Like, that's just not
where I wanted to be.

00:09:31.362 --> 00:09:36.117
That's not where I saw myself
excelling, and it was tough.

00:09:36.117 --> 00:09:37.702
Like, I mean, I was panicking.

00:09:37.702 --> 00:09:41.372
Like, if I was sitting around,
workin' out, staying ready,

00:09:41.372 --> 00:09:43.916
just waiting on a call, stayin'
in touch with Coach Mosley.

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:47.128
Mosley would call me like,
"Yo, I talked to Long Beach.

00:09:47.128 --> 00:09:49.005
They just said this and this and this."

00:09:49.005 --> 00:09:52.341
And I'm getting hype and
waiting, waiting, waiting,

00:09:52.341 --> 00:09:54.969
just sittin'. And then
randomly, out of nowhere

00:09:56.262 --> 00:09:57.722
Long Beach called and told me like,

00:09:57.722 --> 00:10:00.224
"Yo, like, come on. We want you," like.

00:10:00.224 --> 00:10:01.225
- [Yeboah:] Wow.

00:10:01.225 --> 00:10:03.227
- [Hampton:] Yes. We moved
there. And like, let's go.

00:10:03.227 --> 00:10:06.522
And I'm like, ooh, we
goin' to Long Beach!

00:10:06.522 --> 00:10:10.109
- I need to know, what
was in those churros, man?

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.446
What was in those churros, bro?

00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:15.615
I need to know what was in the churros.

00:10:15.615 --> 00:10:17.533
Do you understand how much I love churros?

00:10:22.038 --> 00:10:25.166
- Excuse my language, man, but I
have to say it was crack in 'em churros, man.

00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:27.835
[Both laughing]

00:10:30.671 --> 00:10:35.301
- I'm sayin'.
- Those things were so good.
I don't know what he did,

00:10:35.301 --> 00:10:36.510
like the guy who made 'em,

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:39.472
like he owned this little
churro business or whatever,

00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:42.350
and it was bomb. Like, he had this like...

00:10:44.101 --> 00:10:46.270
caramel, strawberry drizzle.

00:10:47.229 --> 00:10:48.856
- It looked good.

00:10:48.856 --> 00:10:51.108
- It was filled, it was crazy. It's a lot.

00:10:51.108 --> 00:10:53.110
And if, like, if you got a sweet tooth,

